<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Han Chinese</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Han Chinese are the majority ethnic group of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, taking their name from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a>. They were the core population of native dynasties such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> they were ruled by Mongol and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> elites, a relationship that shaped governance and, in the Qing case, nationalist opposition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/han-chinese.jpg" alt="Han Chinese" width="320" height="337" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%AD%A6%E5%AE%98%E8%82%96%E5%83%8F.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
